     ---                                                                        
                                                                                
     ## Generating a Manhattan Plot — Two Paths                                 
                                                                                
     Depending on your GWAS method, you have two routes:                        
                                                                                
     ### Route 1: From PLINK GWAS (fast, linear regression)                     
                                                                                
     If you've already run PLINK --linear (or want to start from scratch),      
     use the **plink-gwas** skill:                                              
                                                                                
     ```                                                                        
     # Step 1: Run GWAS                                                         
     bash                                                                       
     /workspace/pigbole/.piggpa/skills/piggpa-G/plink-gwas/scripts/PLINK-GW     
     AS-linear.sh \                                                             
       --bfile your_genotype_prefix \                                           
       --pheno your_phenotype.tsv \                                             
       --out results/my_gwas                                                    
                                                                                
     # Step 2: Generate Manhattan + QQ plots                                    
     conda activate R                                                           
     Rscript                                                                    
     /workspace/pigbole/.piggpa/skills/piggpa-G/plink-gwas/scripts/PLINK-GW     
     AS-linear-plot.R \                                                         
       --plink_assoc_file results/my_gwas.assoc.linear \                        
       --output_prefix results/my_gwas                                          
     ```                                                                        
                                                                                
     **Outputs:**                                                               
     - `my_gwas_manhattan.pdf` / `my_gwas_manhattan.png` — Manhattan plot       
     - `my_gwas_qq.pdf` / `my_gwas_qq.png` — QQ plot                            
     - `my_gwas_significant_snps.csv` — SNPs at P < 5e-8                        
     - `my_gwas_suggestive_snps.csv` — SNPs at 5e-8 ≤ P < 1e-5                  
     - `my_gwas_summary.txt` / `_summary-zh.txt` — Summary stats                
                                                                                
     ---                                                                        
                                                                                
     ### Route 2: From GCTA MLMA (mixed model, corrects for population          
     structure)                                                                 
                                                                                
     If you need mixed-model correction or already used GCTA, the               
     **gcta-gwas** skill does the full pipeline:                                
                                                                                
     ```                                                                        
     # One-liner: GRM build + GWAS + plots                                      
     bash                                                                       
     /workspace/pigbole/.piggpa/skills/piggpa-G/gcta-gwas/scripts/gcta_gwas     
     _pipeline.sh \                                                             
       --bfile your_genotype_prefix \                                           
       --pheno your_phenotype.tsv \                                             
       --out results/my_mlma_gwas                                               
     ```                                                                        
                                                                                
     Same output format as above, but .mlma files instead of .assoc.linear.     
                                                                                
     ---                                                                        
                                                                                
     ### What the Plots Show                                                    
                                                                                
     | Feature | PLINK GWAS | GCTA MLMA |                                       
     |---------|-----------|-----------|                                        
     | X-axis | Chromosome position, alternating colors per chr | Same |        
     | Y-axis | -log₁₀(P-value) | Same |                                        
     | Orange dashed line | Genome-wide significance (P = 5e-8, y ≈ 7.30) |     
     Same |                                                                     
     | Teal dotted line | Suggestive significance (P = 1e-5, y = 5.0) |         
     Same |                                                                     
     | Title | Includes genomic inflation factor λ | Includes trait name +      
     λ |                                                                        
     | Controls pop structure? | No | Yes (via GRM) |                           
                                                                                
     **What to check in your Manhattan plot:**                                  
     - Peaks above the orange line → significant associations                   
     - Multiple peaks across chromosomes → polygenic architecture               
     - One enormous peak → possible major gene or artifact                      
     - If QQ plot shows early/sustained deviation from diagonal →               
     population stratification (use GCTA MLMA instead)                          
                                                                                
     ---                                                                        
                                                                                
     ### Quick Decision Guide                                                   
                                                                                
     | Your situation | Use |                                                   
     |---------------|-----|                                                    
     | Homogeneous population, quick scan | PLINK GWAS |                        
     | Structured population, related individuals | GCTA MLMA |                 
     | λ > 1.1 from PLINK results | Switch to GCTA MLMA |                       
                                                                                
